WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.770
Endurance. I actually
love endurance training.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.610
I used to do it primarily.

3
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.170
That was like the main way that
I got fitness a number of years

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.210
ago, you know, and I was like,
that's what I did, endurance.

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.930
And I realized something and
I realized it the hard way.

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.730
Okay, I'm going to share this
truly personal story with you.

7
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.770
So first time I went out on one
of these group bike rides, okay,

8
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.370
I was training for a triathlon.

9
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.530
Don't judge me. It's
just what I was doing.

10
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.690
I got out on this group training
ride and we pull over at our

11
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.570
first kind of rest stop, if you
will, which is just like a gas

12
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.770
station. You know, everybody's
going to kind of get out of the

13
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.970
saddle and just kind of rest
themselves for a minute.

14
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.130
And everybody starts pulling all
this fuel out: gels and bars and

15
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.760
all these things.
And I pull out a donut.

16
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.560
Good old-fashioned glazed donut.

17
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.250
And somebody's like, what is that?

18
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.470
And I was like, this is
a warm, tasty pastry.

19
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.130
And somebody goes,

20
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.140
you're going to need
better fuel than that.

21
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.790
Now you know what
I didn't realize?

22
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.500
How much that would apply to
my spiritual life one day.

23
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.170
Because I didn't come to faith
until I was almost 40 years old.

24
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.810
So I fueled my soul with all
sorts of things: obsessions,

25
00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.310
compulsions,

26
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.330
prized possessions, right?

27
00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.730
Accomplishments, corner
offices, big fancy jobs.

28
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.210
I fueled my soul with
all sorts of things.

29
00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.130
And you know what?

30
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.320
That's just like the glazed donut.

31
00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.620
See, I need a clean
fuel for my soul.

32
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.180
And that fuel can only
come from one source.

33
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.980
And that source is God.

34
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.900
Heavenly Father, Lord, I love you.

35
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.900
Just so grateful for you, God.

36
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.340
I'm grateful for what you're doing,
Lord, in our hearts and how

37
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:54.740
you are just reshaping
us every single day.

38
00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:59.300
Lord, I'm so grateful for the
hope that we have, that we

39
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.460
can place in you, God, through
the endurance workouts of life.

40
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.720
And God, we can recognize

41
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.270
that there are fuel sources
for our soul that are literally

42
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.650
glazed donuts.

43
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.430
And there is so
much more available.

44
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.150
And that's why today we're just
taking in these nutrients of

45
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.010
worship and gratitude.

46
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.670
And these are the sources, God,
that we want to draw on as your

47
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.630
Spirit transforms
us so that we might

48
00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:38.050
have the durability and the
resiliency to remain faithful

49
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.750
in the challenges of life.

50
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.686
In Jesus' name, amen.

